# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / Cargo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/target/
**/target/
# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored: this crate builds a Python
# extension (cdylib), not a library consumed by other crates, so the lock
# file is committed for reproducible wheel builds.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUDA / native build artifacts (csrc/ compiled objects)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.obj
*.ptx
*.cubin
*.fatbin
*.so
*.pyd
*.dll
*.dylib
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.i
*.ii
*.gpu
nvcc_error.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheelhouse/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.whl
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maturin
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/custom_cuda/_native*.so
/custom_cuda/_native*.pyd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark & profiling outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
benchmarks/**/*.csv
benchmarks/**/*.json
benchmarks/results/
*.nsys-rep
*.ncu-rep
*.sqlite
*.qdrep

# CLI `profile` command output (Chrome trace JSON files)
/profiles/

# Note: visualizations/**/*.png|svg were previously ignored here as
# "regeneratable build artifacts," same as the benchmark CSVs above.
# That's wrong for this repo: the README embeds specific chart files as
# the finished, showcased deliverable, not raw data — they need to be
# committed for the repo to render correctly on GitHub. Charts are
# tracked; regenerate via `custom_cuda_cli visualize <kernel>` or
# `scripts/plot_*.py` if the underlying benchmark data changes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
